; heading keeps the candidate whose line makes the smallest angle with the
; given line (ADR 0031). Of the two tangents through .p, the one at 45° is
; nearer the bottom edge's direction than the vertical one, and it lands .d
; at the centre.

paper square
mark (map .a onto .b) as --ef
mark (through .b .d) as --bd
.p = free on --bd from .d at 1/4
fold (align (.d onto --ef) (through .p) (heading --ab))

; assert steps = 1
; assert .d = (1/2, 1/2)
